"Chris Randle" <chris@amlog.co.uk> wrote:

> Also, from a role-playing perspective, if a knight, say, would never
> dream of stealing anything, what should he do with the item that his
> pet has taken from the store?
> 
He should return the item to the shopkeeper (with his apologies for the 
rude behaviour of the pet). If the shopkeeper insists on rewarding him for 
his trouble the correct action is to accept the reward politely but donate 
it to charity (i.e. give it to a priest).


